CHANGE 1, section "## 7. BOUNDARIES AND FLOW", the "Imports" row. Its cell currently starts "`lib/` cores import Node builtins only. Adapters import their own `../lib/` and `../../shared/hook-flags.mjs` (or `hook-flags.cjs` for the OpenCode plugin): nothing outside this tree." That is wrong for Pi: `pi/dispatch-preflight-lint.ts` and `pi/dispatch-audit.ts` import `../../.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.mjs`, a path written against their `.pi/extensions/` symlink, because Pi resolves an extension's relative imports from the symlink path. Insert, directly after the sentence ending "nothing outside this tree.", this sentence:

The Pi adapters are the exception: they import `../../.skilled/hooks/shared/hook-flags.mjs`, a path written for their `.pi/extensions/` symlink, so a test loads them only under `.skilled/hooks/vitest.config.ts`, whose alias maps that path to the real tree.

Keep the rest of the cell unchanged and keep the table row on one line.

